EVEN runners {2,4,6,8,10,12} at t=1/14 (= 7th roots minus origin):
  |alpha_j| = [np.float64(0.1667), np.float64(0.2), np.float64(0.25), np.float64(0.3333), np.float64(0.5), np.float64(1.0)]
  harmonic 1/(7-1-j)=1/(6-j): [0.1667, 0.2, 0.25, 0.3333, 0.5, 1.0]  MATCH? True
  => the EVEN sub-cloud IS the n=7 harmonic law: a recursive LRC(7) inside LRC(14).  alpha_0=1/6 (centroid from origin).

ODD runners [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13] at t=1/14 (= full z^7=-1 heptagon, 7 pts):
  |alpha_j| = [np.float64(0.0), np.float64(0.0), np.float64(0.0), np.float64(0.0), np.float64(0.0), np.float64(0.0)]  (uniform on a full rotated heptagon => Verblunsky ~0 then terminal 1 = SYMMETRIC/Haar)
  => the ODD sub-cloud = the SC D_7 tournament's Cayley-dual (7th roots), Verblunsky (0..0,1).

== THE DECOMPOSITION (14 = 2 x 7, CRT) ==
  Z/2 (parity) = iota = the COMPLEMENT/antipode symmetry (splits odd vs even runners)
  Z/7 (heptagon) = D_7 = the tournament vertices / 7th roots
  ODD half  -> full heptagon z^7=-1  -> SC rotational tournament (Aut C_7, 14 triangles) -Cayley-> 7th roots, Verblunsky (0..0,1)
  EVEN half -> z^7=+1 minus origin   -> HARMONIC Verblunsky 1/(6-j) = sub-LRC(7)
  => LRC(14)'s lonely config FACTORS as (parity Z/2) x (heptagon D_7): the repo's Mode-B/CRT descent, made concrete.
